1
00:00:01,870 --> 00:00:09,200
Introducers & Partners
Brokers, agents and professionals who refer clients for a commission — from onboarding to the commission they earn.

2
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:11,960
Anil Bhugaloo, a notary in Port Louis, wants to refer clients to Genesis
Every introducer is first a party — the same record KYC is run on

3
00:00:11,960 --> 00:00:17,680
Sign in as Shalini Ramtohul — Head of BD & Strategic Partnerships
Head of BD — onboards and manages introducers

4
00:00:17,680 --> 00:00:26,240
Clients ▸ Parties ▸ New: identity and contact details

5
00:00:26,240 --> 00:00:33,760
Growth ▸ Introducers ▸ Introducer onboarding
A two-step wizard: who the introducer is, then the agreement and commission plan

6
00:00:33,760 --> 00:00:37,240
The portal email is how the introducer will sign in to the introducer portal

7
00:00:37,240 --> 00:00:42,920
Agreement & commission: the agreement is not signed yet
Choose the products the introducer may refer; clawback and protection window keep their defaults

8
00:00:42,920 --> 00:00:46,240
Introducer created at Applied — complete KYC to activate
An introducer number is given automatically

9
00:00:46,320 --> 00:00:51,468
Onboarding pipeline: Applied ▸ KYC ▸ Agreement ▸ Active
Move the new introducer to KYC while the documents are collected

10
00:00:51,468 --> 00:00:59,548
Now try Agreement…
The agreement stage needs the signature date and the commission rate

11
00:00:59,588 --> 00:01:08,108
The agreement is signed: record the date, expiry and commission rate
0.4% of the funded or disbursed volume

12
00:01:08,108 --> 00:01:12,068
Move to Agreement again — this time it goes through

13
00:01:12,068 --> 00:01:20,068
Activate the introducer…
The CRM checks the introducer’s own KYC first

14
00:01:20,068 --> 00:01:21,548
Blocked: KYC is not approved yet
The legitimate way: a KYC case on the introducer, signed off by Compliance

15
00:01:21,588 --> 00:01:27,868
KYC & Compliance ▸ KYC Cases ▸ New
Group-level KYC on the introducer — the same process as for a client (Tutorial 18)

16
00:01:27,868 --> 00:01:35,588
ID, proof of address and source of funds are on file
Tick the checks and the FATCA status

17
00:01:35,588 --> 00:01:42,948
Move it to Screening: sanctions and PEP lists are checked automatically

18
00:01:42,948 --> 00:01:46,988
Screening is clear — Pending approval sends the case to Compliance

19
00:01:47,228 --> 00:02:00,588
Sign in as Fatima Hossenbux — Compliance Officer
Compliance officer — signs off KYC

20
00:02:00,628 --> 00:02:00,948
Back to the Head of BD: activate the introducer
KYC approved and agreement signed — the gate lets it through

21
00:02:00,948 --> 00:02:11,935
Sign in as Shalini Ramtohul — Head of BD & Strategic Partnerships
Head of BD

22
00:02:11,935 --> 00:02:16,375
Anil Bhugaloo is active: KYC approved, agreement and commission on file
Only an active introducer can sign in to the introducer portal

23
00:02:16,375 --> 00:02:20,615
Meanwhile, Hemraj Ah-Kye — an active broker — has a client to refer
He uses the introducer portal: /portal/genesis-capital

24
00:02:20,615 --> 00:02:22,855
Choose Introducer and enter the portal email Genesis holds
No password: a one-time code is sent by email

25
00:02:22,855 --> 00:02:28,295
Outside production the code is shown on screen
In production it arrives by email and expires after 10 minutes

26
00:02:28,295 --> 00:02:31,375
His referrals and commissions — only his own
A referral’s status is shown only where the prospect agreed to share it

27
00:02:31,375 --> 00:02:40,415
Refer a client: Mélanie Rault needs a personal loan

28
00:02:40,415 --> 00:02:44,695
She agreed that Hemraj may follow her application
So the portal will show him its status

29
00:02:44,695 --> 00:02:48,372
The referral is in — Submitted
It lands in the CRM at once

30
00:02:48,372 --> 00:02:50,513
Back in the CRM, the Head of BD sees the referral
Growth ▸ Introducers ▸ Introducer Referrals

31
00:02:50,513 --> 00:02:59,177
The CRM created an enquiry for the prospect, credited to the introducer
Attribution is protected for 90 days from submission

32
00:02:59,177 --> 00:03:06,017
The enquiry: channel Introducer, linked to Hemraj
Credited to him for the attribution window

33
00:03:06,017 --> 00:03:10,377
Routed by product like any other enquiry: Retail Loans, to Yash Bholah
Loans Executive — the speed-to-lead clock starts now

34
00:03:10,377 --> 00:03:19,277
As the desk works the enquiry, BD moves the referral along
Submitted ▸ Accepted ▸ In progress ▸ Funded / disbursed

35
00:03:19,277 --> 00:03:28,677
The loan is disbursed — try Funded / disbursed…
The CRM needs the funded amount to work out the commission

36
00:03:28,677 --> 00:03:36,903
Record the amount actually disbursed: MUR 1,400,000

37
00:03:37,023 --> 00:03:41,863
Funded: the commission is accrued automatically
Hemraj Ah-Kye’s rate 0.5% × MUR 1,400,000 = MUR 7,000

38
00:03:41,863 --> 00:03:44,863
Status Accrued — Finance approves and pays it, then marks it Paid
The introducer sees it under Commissions in the portal

39
00:03:44,863 --> 00:03:49,579
A client repaid a referred personal loan early, within the 12-month clawback period
The commission paid to Hemraj Ah-Kye in June is clawed back

40
00:03:49,579 --> 00:03:54,139
Clawed-back commission no longer counts as earned
Commission earned on the introducer is recalculated

41
00:03:54,179 --> 00:04:00,219
Dashboard ▸ Marketing: the introducer channel at a glance
Referrals by stage and commission by status

42
00:04:00,219 --> 00:04:04,299
Referrals by stage — from submitted to funded
Commission by status: accrued, approved, paid and clawed back

43
00:04:08,745 --> 00:04:16,419
Introducers & Partners
Partners are onboarded with the same rigour as clients, and every referral is traceable to the commission it earns.
